    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.resize\n\n### Description\n\nA sub-plugin like [smart-splits.nvim](https://github.com/mrjones2014/smart-splits.nvim) helps people easily resize their windows.\r\nNeovim isn't a gui software thus resizing the windows is troublesome. This feature is simple but useful.\r\n\r\nExpected behaviors (like smart-splits.nvim):\r\n1. Normally it doesn't map any key to resize since people generally don't need to resize the windows. \r\n3. It creates the resize-mode which allows us to resize the windows by h/j/k/l.\r\n\r\nI can help you implement this sub-plugin if you want it in mini.nvim. Of course, it is totally ok if you want to implement it by yourself.",
